HST Office: booklet (saddle-stitch) PDF export, imposed by the PDF filter.

A new PDF export option lays the exported pages out two per sheet side in folding order, so one PDF
can be printed double-sided on any printer or at a print shop and folded into a booklet:
- FilterData "Booklet" (boolean, default false) for every *_pdf_Export filter (Writer, Sheets, Slides,
  Draw, also a PDF opened in Draw), from macros/UNO, the command line JSON filter options, and a new
  "Booklet" checkbox in the Range section of the PDF Options dialog (General tab). The checkbox is not
  stored in the configuration: each export starts unchecked.
- PDFExport records every page as before but keeps the metafiles; after the whole selection is
  rendered they are placed on sheets: the page count is padded with blank pages to a multiple of 4
  and the sides follow the saddle-stitch order (8 pages: 8|1, 2|7, 6|3, 4|5) for duplex printing
  flipped on the short edge. Placement reuses the N-up technique of the vcl print path (scale, move,
  clip each page to its half); watermarks, PDF/A, transparency removal and redaction keep working
  on the sheets.
- Sheet size: the first page turned by 90 degrees (A4 document -> A4 landscape sheets carrying two
  A5-sized pages, the same paper as the document). FilterData "BookletKeepPageSize" (boolean) instead
  makes the sheet two pages at 100 % (A5 document -> A4 sheets). Portrait pages sit side by side;
  landscape pages are stacked on a portrait sheet (fold on the horizontal centre line).
- A booklet is for printing: tags, PDF/UA, links, outlines, comment annotations, form fields and
  slide transitions are not exported in this mode (they address document pages, which the
  imposed file no longer has).
- vi filter/messages.po: the Vietnamese label and tip.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_filter_pdf (testBookletEightPages, testBookletFivePages: page count padded to a
multiple of 4, sheet size, page order on each sheet side).
